Z||000010||Spektrum-87GT||11-04-2001||04:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bocefas:<BR><B>Not to be a wet blanket, but if you would have seen cars running around like that on Sept. 10th, you probably would've thought they were wierd.  I'm as patriotic as the next guy, it's just a shame that it takes a tragedy like Sept. 11 for people to feel comfortable showing some pride in the USA...I wonder how many of them even bothered to vote in the last presidential election.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i have to agree, the whole flag thing is ashame. people were storming stores to buy as many as possible, then turning around and selling them on street corners and ebay for up to and over 100 bucks for a decent sized flag. the same bandwagon soccer moms that sport 'obx'(would understand if you live on the east coast) and the infamous soccer ball stickers have replaced them with american flags. I'm all for being patriotic, but when you're patriotic to fit in with the crowd, jump on the bandwagon, or because its the 'hip thing to do', it makes me sick. i work with a guy that was in vietnam, and in the army for over 20 years, he would not shutup about how pathetic it was using a symbol like the american flag like it was(and still is) being used. as a side note, i work down in an area with high crime, and the same crackheads selling drugs on the corner started to sell anything and everything with the american flag on it. end mission ranting.<BR>||||reg||1
